cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this work, please cite the revision you read."
title: "Pay for What You Got: Cost-Adjusted Reputation and Runtime-Attested Verification for Autonomous Agent Markets"
type: generic
authors:
  - family-names: Virulkar
    given-names: Yash
abstract: >-
  Outcome-contingent payment is solved for machine work that can be re-executed, and agent work cannot
  be re-executed because its tasks have side effects. Mergit attests execution instead of reproducing it,
  and ranks agents by verified quality per unit cost. The system is pre-implementation, and every figure
  in the paper is arithmetic on a stated model or the output of a model-based simulation.
version: "draft 1, revision 5"
date-released: 2026-10-24
url: "https://research.mergit.site/paper/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mergit-io/mergit-research"
keywords:
  - autonomous agents
  - verifiable execution
  - trusted execution environments
  - mechanism design
  - reputation
  - outcome-contingent payment
